(A voting machine has three candidates. Option 1 adds a vote to Candidate A, option 2 adds a vote to Candidate B, option) Tj
T* (3 resets both candidates' votes, and every other input increases the invalid vote count. What is the final output?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (```cpp) Tj
T* (int A = 0, B = 0, invalid = 0;) Tj
T* (int choice[] = {1, 2, 1, 4, 2, 3, 1, 5, 2, 4};) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (for \(int i = 0; i < 10; i++\) {) Tj
T* (    switch \(choice[i]\) {) Tj
T* (        case 1:) Tj
T* (            A++;) Tj
T* (            break;) Tj
T* (        case 2:) Tj
T* (            B++;) Tj
T* (            break;) Tj
T* (        case 3:) Tj
T* (            A = 0;) Tj
T* (            B = 0;) Tj
T* (            break;) Tj
T* (        default:) Tj
T* (            invalid++;) Tj
T* (    }) Tj
T* (}) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (cout << A << " " << B << " " << invalid;) Tj
T* (```) Tj
